value.REFLECTION_MODE.0=Sky only
value.REFLECTION_MODE.1=Reference
value.REFLECTION_MODE.2=High
option.SKY_AMBIENT=Diffuse ambient brightness
option.SKY_AMBIENT.comment=Diffuse skylight brightness. Expanded range reaches very dark and deliberately bright looks; source default1.40.
option.ambientOcclusionLevel=Corner shading
option.ambientOcclusionLevel.comment=Vanilla corner AO, default and maximum 1.00; does not raise exposure.
option.WHITE_BALANCE=Subtle white balance
option.WHITE_BALANCE.comment=Zero preserves neutral foreground colour.
option.SURFACE_SATURATION=Surface saturation
option.SURFACE_SATURATION.comment=1.00 preserves the input saturation before enhanced lighting and bloom. Vanilla lighting bypasses this artistic adjustment.
option.SURFACE_DAMPNESS=Surface film amount
option.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.comment=Thin exposed water film on porous and non-porous solid blocks. No absorption darkening or retained dampness. Zero disables film; existing saved values are retained.
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.00=Dry
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.35=Subtle
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.0.65=Moderate
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.00=Normal (default)
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.35=Strong
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.1.70=Very strong
value.SURFACE_DAMPNESS.2.00=Maximum
option.LAMP_LEVEL=Lantern and block light
option.LAMP_LEVEL.comment=Diffuse local brightness and emissive pixel interiors, with adjustable subtle bloom.
option.LAMP_HEAT=Local light warmth
option.LAMP_HEAT.comment=A restrained amber bias where block lighting dominates.
option.CLOUD_AMOUNT=Overcast coverage
option.CLOUD_AMOUNT.comment=Density/coverage strength of the current vanilla cloud footprint. Zero hides the lower layer; high clouds are independent. The footprint is preserved at every nonzero value.
option.CLOUD_SPAN=Cloud band size
option.CLOUD_SPAN.comment=Scale of the current vanilla cloud footprint. Default 240 gives 12-block texture cells; changing scale preserves its connected shapes.
option.CLOUD_DISTORTION=Cloud shape irregularity
option.CLOUD_DISTORTION.comment=Gentle vertical relief within connected clouds. Never warps or erodes the vanilla horizontal footprint.
option.CLOUD_RELIEF=Cloud shade depth
option.CLOUD_RELIEF.comment=Self-shadowing and smooth light/dark depth within the simple connected cloud forms.
option.CLOUD_DRIFT=Slow cloud drift
option.CLOUD_DRIFT.comment=Zero freezes the world-anchored ceiling.
option.CLOUD_LAYERS=Cloud sampling
option.CLOUD_LAYERS.comment=Cloud integration and self-shadow sampling. Source default follows your recorded Main preference; every quality choice remains available.
option.MIST_AMOUNT=Valley mist density
option.MIST_AMOUNT.comment=Outdoor mist opacity. Cave surfaces without skylight reject valley mist.
option.MIST_Y=Lower mist altitude
option.MIST_Y.comment=World Y of the principal pale horizontal mist layer.
option.MIST_THICKNESS=Mist layer thickness
option.MIST_THICKNESS.comment=Height/depth of drifting3D fog pockets and valley layers, adjustable from thin banks to deep mist.
option.MIST_CLEAR=Clear foreground range
option.MIST_CLEAR.comment=Clear range before volumetric fog begins. Default24blocks lets nearby pockets show depth while the immediate foreground remains clear.
option.MIST_DETAIL=Mist spatial variation
option.MIST_DETAIL.comment=Sampling detail for broad horizontal density patches.
option.REFLECT_LEVEL=Water reflection amount
option.REFLECT_LEVEL.comment=Scales above-water angle-dependent dielectric reflection. 1.00 uses physical Fresnel. The underwater interface remains transparent without a reflection overlay.
option.REFLECTION_MODE=Scenery reflection quality
option.REFLECTION_MODE.comment=Sky fallback,32-step scenery tracing, or96-step high-quality tracing with precise hits. Hidden geometry remains a screen-space limitation.
option.REFLECT_RANGE=Scenery trace distance
option.REFLECT_RANGE.comment=Misses fade to the procedural sky, including at screen borders.
option.WATER_VISIBILITY=Water clarity
option.WATER_VISIBILITY.comment=1.70 is the default. Higher values reduce optical extinction. Actual visibility also responds to biome sediment, rain runoff and shelter. Used by Stratus water appearance; saved tuning is retained while Vanilla uses game fog.
option.WATER_EXTINCTION=Depth absorption
option.WATER_EXTINCTION.comment=Absorption and sediment scattering along the actual water segment. Underwater fog stops at the visible exit; air beyond it adds no water absorption. Used by Stratus water appearance; saved tuning is retained while Vanilla uses game fog.
option.RIPPLE_HEIGHT=Ripple strength
option.RIPPLE_HEIGHT.comment=Shading normal amplitude. Water geometry remains vanilla.
option.RIPPLE_SIZE=Ripple spacing
option.RIPPLE_SIZE.comment=Scale of the four unequal spectral wave components.
option.RIPPLE_RATE=Ripple speed
option.RIPPLE_RATE.comment=Zero freezes all surface movement.
option.FACE_SHADING=Combined face contrast
option.FACE_SHADING.comment=Master strength for vanilla and realistic components. Both new component multipliers at 1 reproduce the previous combined look.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Subtle bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Visible restrained light halos. Emissive masking protects ordinary entities and white blocks from glowing.
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE=Physical cloud altitude
option.CLOUD_ALTITUDE.comment=World height of the cloud layer centre. Fly below, through and above it.
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS=Physical cloud thickness
option.CLOUD_THICKNESS.comment=Vertical thickness in blocks. Default 12 keeps connected vanilla shapes low and simple; 4 approaches vanilla slab proportions. Existing thicker values remain available.
option.SKY_LEAK=Light through the sky
option.SKY_LEAK.comment=Broad daylight glow through the cloud ceiling. Sun visibility separately controls the haze-softened solar core.
option.WET_SHEEN=Wet sheen strength
option.WET_SHEEN.comment=View-dependent highlights on exposed solid blocks, including metal and glazed materials. Works with either lighting mode. Zero disables sheen; sealed caves remain dry.
option.BLOOM_RADIUS=Bloom radius
option.BLOOM_RADIUS.comment=Restrained halo width, stable relative to image height. Bloom strength remains a separate control.
option.SUN_VISIBILITY=Sun through overcast
option.SUN_VISIBILITY.comment=Brightness of the polished blocky sun behind clouds. Zero hides its textured core; broad sky haze remains.
option.FACE_BLEND=Face shading blend
option.FACE_BLEND.comment=Combined face-component blend in realistic lighting mode. Zero bypasses the two components; vanilla lighting mode uses the game lighting directly.
option.GROUND_WARMTH=Sun-warmed ground
option.GROUND_WARMTH.comment=Golden sunlight only on outward sun-facing block faces, weighted by skylight and nearby visible occluders. No brown tint on all sides.
option.WATER_DISTORTION=Above-water refraction distortion
option.WATER_DISTORTION.comment=Controls the ripple distortion seen through water from above. Underwater uses a straight-through view without Snell refraction; Ripple height adjusts the shared surface shape.
option.CIRRUS_AMOUNT=High cloud coverage
option.CIRRUS_AMOUNT.comment=Coverage/strength of the independent high cloud veil. Its separate density control makes the layer visible without changing lower clouds. Zero hides the upper layer.
option.CIRRUS_ALTITUDE=High cloud altitude
option.CIRRUS_ALTITUDE.comment=World altitude of the upper wispy cloud layer.
screen.WATER=Water
screen.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
screen.WAVES=Ripples
screen.LIGHTING=Lighting
screen.CLOUDS=Clouds
screen.SUN=Sun and moon
screen.FOG=Fog
screen.MATERIALS=Wet materials
screen.POST=Camera and colour
screen.PERFORMANCE=Performance
option.CLOUD_STYLE=Cloud style
option.CLOUD_STYLE.comment=Stratus extrudes the running game's current cloud texture with simple forms and soft shading. Vanilla uses actual fancy cloud geometry. Off hides both.
value.CLOUD_STYLE.0=Stratus volumetric
value.CLOUD_STYLE.1=Vanilla fancy
value.CLOUD_STYLE.2=Off
option.SUN_STYLE=Sun and moon style
option.SUN_STYLE.comment=Polished mode keeps Minecraft's square sun and adds independently adjustable core brightness and local halo. Vanilla mode retains native textured sun and moon.
value.SUN_STYLE.0=Polished vanilla sun
value.SUN_STYLE.1=Vanilla textures
option.BIOME_WATER=Environment-aware water
option.BIOME_WATER.comment=Vanilla biome tint plus smoothed sediment, humidity, temperature, rain runoff and local cave lighting. These are visual approximations, not measured sediment data. Stratus mode only; Vanilla appearance always uses native vertex biome colours.
value.BIOME_WATER.0=Off
value.BIOME_WATER.1=On
option.WATER_TURBIDITY=Suspended sediment
option.WATER_TURBIDITY.comment=Scattering from suspended particles. Swamps and rainy rivers carry more sediment; sheltered cave water rejects rain runoff. Used by Stratus water appearance; saved tuning is retained while Vanilla uses game fog.
screen.REFRACTION=Refraction
option.REFRACTION_QUALITY=Refraction quality
option.REFRACTION_QUALITY.comment=Higher levels improve shoreline protection above water and the search for terrain viewed through the surface from underwater. Fast retains the original above-water depth guard.
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.REFRACTION_QUALITY.2=High
option.CLOUD_DENSITY=Cloud optical thickness
option.CLOUD_DENSITY.comment=Optical density of the simple cloud volumes. Lower-layer shapes come from the active vanilla/resource-pack cloud texture.
option.CLOUD_DETAIL=Cloud gradient detail
option.CLOUD_DETAIL.comment=Broad smooth density gradients within simple connected clouds. Fine pores and noisy billows have been removed.
option.MIST_SCALE=Fog pocket size
option.MIST_SCALE.comment=World-space size of drifting3D fog banks. Smaller values produce more local pockets; larger values broad valley structures.
option.MIST_BREAKUP=Fog spatial variation
option.MIST_BREAKUP.comment=Zero makes smooth fog; higher values create distinct connected pockets and gaps. Shape remains anchored in3D world space.
option.MIST_LIGHT=Fog light scattering
option.MIST_LIGHT.comment=Directional sunlight scattered by fog, with internal extinction. Independent of fog density.
option.WET_DARKENING=Retired darkening
option.WET_DARKENING.comment=Compatibility setting: saved values remain readable, but this effect was explicitly removed in 1.6.9 to preserve vanilla block colours. Adjust Surface film amount and Wet sheen strength instead.
option.EXPOSURE=Overall exposure
option.EXPOSURE.comment=Camera brightness in stops, affecting terrain, sky, water and bloom together. +1 doubles scene light; HUD is unchanged.
option.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY=Atmosphere quality
option.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.comment=Cloud and fog image quality, independent of water reflections. Balanced retains volume detail at lower rendering cost.
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.ATMOSPHERE_QUALITY.2=High
option.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY=Water render quality
option.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.comment=Resolution of water surface optics. Balanced uses half resolution with depth and normal aware reconstruction. Opaque terrain and submerged blocks seen directly remain full resolution.
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.0=Fast
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.1=Balanced
value.WATER_RENDER_QUALITY.2=Full resolution
option.VANILLA_FACE_CONTRAST=Vanilla face component
option.VANILLA_FACE_CONTRAST.comment=Independent multiplier for fixed vanilla axis contrast. 0 removes it; 1 retains the previous contribution. Existing master contrast/blend remain.
option.REALISTIC_FACE_CONTRAST=Realistic face component
option.REALISTIC_FACE_CONTRAST.comment=Adjusts only the directional face component. Use Realistic lighting: Off to restore vanilla face lighting, lightmap brightness and colour together.
option.SUN_CORE_BRIGHTNESS=Polished sun brightness
option.SUN_CORE_BRIGHTNESS.comment=HDR brightness of the blocky textured core in polished mode. 2.80 reproduces the previous core; vanilla mode is unaffected.
option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH=Sun-local halo strength
option.SUN_HALO_STRENGTH.comment=Additional light scatter around the polished sun only. 0 disables it without altering the core or global bloom.
option.SUN_HALO_RADIUS=Sun-local halo radius
option.SUN_HALO_RADIUS.comment=Angular spread of the polished sun's smoothly falling halo. Does not resize the blocky core or brighten unrelated objects.
option.CIRRUS_DENSITY=High cloud density
option.CIRRUS_DENSITY.comment=Optical density of the independent high cloud layer. 0 hides it; coverage/altitude and lower-cloud controls remain independent.
option.REALISTIC_LIGHTING=Realistic lighting
option.REALISTIC_LIGHTING.comment=Off (default) restores the game's vertex face lighting/AO and lightmap colour/brightness, bypassing ambient/lamp boosts, ground warmth, bloom and camera grading. Independent wet highlights, Stratus water and atmosphere remain. On retains artistic controls; saved settings are preserved.
value.REALISTIC_LIGHTING.0=Off (vanilla, default)
value.REALISTIC_LIGHTING.1=On
option.WET_WEATHER_MODE=Wet sheen conditions
option.WET_WEATHER_MODE.comment=All weather allows exposed film without rain; Rain only gates it by rainfall. Surface film amount, exposure and face drainage control the highlights. Both porous and non-porous blocks are supported in either lighting mode.
value.WET_WEATHER_MODE.0=All weather
value.WET_WEATHER_MODE.1=Rain only
screen.FACE_LIGHTING=Face shading
screen.FACE_LIGHTING.comment=Independent face components and combined strength. Used in realistic lighting mode.
screen.AMBIENT_LIGHT=Ambient and daylight
screen.AMBIENT_LIGHT.comment=Ambient level, corner AO and sun warmth. Vanilla mode retains the game lightmap and skips artistic brightness/warmth changes.
screen.BLOCK_LIGHT=Block light
screen.BLOCK_LIGHT.comment=Local brightness and warmth for Stratus lighting.
screen.CLOUD_SHAPE=Cloud shape and movement
screen.CLOUD_SHAPE.comment=Advanced lower-cloud scale, gradients, relief and drift. The vanilla footprint remains intact.
screen.CIRRUS=High clouds
screen.CIRRUS.comment=Independent cirrus coverage, optical density and altitude.
screen.COLOUR=Exposure and colour
screen.COLOUR.comment=Camera grading for Stratus lighting. Saved values remain when vanilla lighting bypasses grading.
screen.BLOOM=Bloom
screen.BLOOM.comment=Global light halos. The polished sun also has independent local halo controls.
option.WATER_TEXTURE=Vanilla water texture
option.WATER_TEXTURE.comment=In Vanilla mode this also controls the animated underside seen from underwater. Native animated still/flow contribution across the whole visible surface. In Vanilla appearance it controls native surface colour/alpha; zero removes that layer. In Stratus appearance it controls the retained patterned biome tint. Reflection/refraction settings remain independent.

option.WATER_STYLE=Water appearance
option.WATER_STYLE.comment=Vanilla uses the active still/flow texture, biome colour, light and game underwater fog, with Stratus reflections/refraction retained. Stratus restores depth-based absorption and clarity tuning.
value.WATER_STYLE.0=Stratus
value.WATER_STYLE.1=Vanilla
screen.TRANSPARENT_OPTICS=Transparent solids
screen.TRANSPARENT_OPTICS.comment=Thin-surface optics for glass, panes, ice, honey and slime. Native colour/alpha remain; screen-space data cannot reveal hidden scenery or every overlapping layer.
option.TRANSPARENT_REFLECTIONS=Solid reflections
option.TRANSPARENT_REFLECTIONS.comment=View-dependent reflections on transparent solid faces. Uses current reflection quality and sky fallback. Zero disables them independently of wet film and water.
option.TRANSPARENT_REFRACTION=Solid refraction
option.TRANSPARENT_REFRACTION.comment=Subtle face-normal refraction on transparent solids, with depth and screen-edge guards. No animated water waves. Zero disables refraction without removing reflections.
